[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2872307327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2872307327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2872307327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rM-5_","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T12:09:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T12:09:30Z","body":"> later spawn another CharacterBody3D at anywhere in the scene\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready()->void :\n\tchar1 = char_pre.instantiate()\n\tadd_child(char1)\n\tchar1.position = Vector3.ZERO\n\n\tawait get_tree().create_timer(1).timeout\n\tchar2 = char_pre.instantiate()\n\tadd_child(char2)\n\tchar2.position = Vector3.ONE\n```\n\nYou spawned the CharacterBody3D __at__ (0,0) first and then moved it. Try setting `position` before calling `add_child()`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2872307327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2872569358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2872569358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2872569358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rN-4O","user":{"login":"silderan","id":10522542,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIyNTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10522542?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan","html_url":"https://github.com/silderan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T13:25:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T13:25:17Z","body":"> > later spawn another CharacterBody3D at anywhere in the scene\n> \n> func _ready()->void :\n> \tchar1 = char_pre.instantiate()\n> \tadd_child(char1)\n> \tchar1.position = Vector3.ZERO\n> \n> \tawait get_tree().create_timer(1).timeout\n> \tchar2 = char_pre.instantiate()\n> \tadd_child(char2)\n> \tchar2.position = Vector3.ONE\n> You spawned the CharacterBody3D **at** (0,0) first and then moved it. Try setting `position` before calling `add_child()`.\n\nDone and the first character doesn't jumps. But this is a circumstantial workaround for this test code.\nAlso, I know it's hard to hit this issue in \"real world\" because there MUST BE a CharacterBody3D very close to (0,0,0) when instantiating another one elsewhere.\nBut, the bug is there and may struggle someone trying to find a bug on in their very own code (like me XD)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2872569358/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875222944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2875222944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2875222944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rYGug","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T06:37:10Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T06:37:10Z","body":"This is expected behavior as both the first and the second character are at (0,0) after the `add_child(char2)` call. One of them will be pushed away so they don't overlap.\n\nIn other words, this is a bug in user code instead of the engine.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2875222944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876427429","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2876427429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2876427429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rcsyl","user":{"login":"silderan","id":10522542,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIyNTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10522542?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan","html_url":"https://github.com/silderan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T13:00:59Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T13:00:59Z","body":"You're completely right.\n\nAfter thinking it through more deeply, I now understand what's going on and why it's considered an \"expected\" behavior:\n\nWhen instantiating multiple CharacterBody3D scenes at the same position, the previously instantiated ones seem to jump on top of the new ones, like a rider mounting a horse. So when the new one is moved in the same frame, it carries the old one along with it. This is due to the physics engine automatically resolving the overlap by treating it as a standing-on-top situation.\n\nIn my opinion, while this might be \"expected\" from the engine's perspective, it's not exactly \"desired\" from a developer's point of view.\n\nWhat makes this behavior even more counterintuitive is that:\n\n- It doesn't happen if both bodies are instantiated in the same frame,\n- The overlap resolution happens immediately upon entering the scene tree, even before any physics step.\n- Setting a position on an object before it's in the scene tree (i.e. before add_child()) is something I've always tried to avoid. It just feels unnatural — though clearly, in this case, it's the right thing to do.\n\nAll that said, I realize this is probably an edge case, easily worked around, and maybe difficult to solve internally without side effects. So I totally understand if it's left as-is.\n\nThanks for the clarification!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2876427429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2884010084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2884010084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2884010084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6r5oBk","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-15T14:24:40Z","updated_at":"2025-05-15T14:24:40Z","body":"> This is expected behavior\n>...\n>All that said, I realize this is probably an edge case, easily worked around, and maybe difficult to solve internally without side effects. So I totally understand if it's left as-is.\n\nCan we close or is there anything else that could be optimized?\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2884010084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2886750474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106303#issuecomment-2886750474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106303","id":2886750474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sEFEK","user":{"login":"silderan","id":10522542,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTIyNTQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10522542?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan","html_url":"https://github.com/silderan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/silderan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-16T13:36:04Z","updated_at":"2025-05-16T21:01:56Z","body":"By the way.\nSame issue when ussing global_position. But setting up global_position before add_child displays this error:\n\n```\nE 0:00:01:642   world.gd:10 @ _ready(): Condition \"!is_inside_tree()\" is true. Returning: Transform3D()\n  <C++ Fuente>  scene/3d/node_3d.cpp:466 @ get_global_transform()\n  <Rastreo de Pila>world.gd:10 @ _ready()\n```\nSo, the workarround of setting position before add_child doesn't seems to be the way to go for all cases.\n\nThe best option is to avoid the world origin coordinates to be used by any CharacterBody3D.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2886750474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]